# The exported copy must be byte-identical wherever it was produced, because comparing copies is the
# whole job of the format: one record per line, so a later export differs from an earlier one by
# whole LINES. No rule of the root .gitattributes covers the file, so without this line a clone
# with core.autocrlf=true would hold the sample as CRLF on Windows while CI holds it as LF -- a
# difference on every line, for a reason that has nothing to do with the audit trail, in the one file
# whose only signal is which lines differ.
#
# ExportedSampleTests.The_committed_bytes_are_what_the_tool_writes_on_any_platform asserts the
# absence of CR, so without this the guard would go red on a fresh Windows clone and red for a reason
# no reader could act on. Scoped to this directory deliberately: a rule for every text file at
# the root would renormalise the whole repository in one commit.
*.jsonl text eol=lf
